  "body": "Deadline sale: Closes on Wednesday 9 December 2026 at 4:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nIgnore CV and previous price expectations. Second time on the market, contact the listing agents for a price guide. \r\n\r\nElevated quietly above the water within a boutique, solid concrete block building of just three residences, this north-west facing home frames a commanding panorama from the Sky Tower across the harbour to Rangitoto, North Head and beyond.\r\n\r\nFloor-to-ceiling glass turns the view into a living artwork from both living areas and the main bedroom, while approx. 240m² of elegant, flowing space delivers the scale of a home with the ease of apartment living.\r\n\r\nAt its heart, a beautifully appointed kitchen with abundant storage invites you to entertain against the backdrop of Rangitoto, flowing to two generous living areas, including a formal lounge warmed by a gas fireplace. Outdoors, a generous covered deck sets the scene for alfresco dining and sunset drinks as the harbour drifts by.\r\n\r\nAccommodation comprises a main suite in its own private wing, opening to a covered balcony, with a spacious walk-in wardrobe and a statement bathroom. Two further generous bedrooms each have their own bathroom, one with a bath, the other with private lobby access, ideal as a home office.\r\n\r\nFurther highlights include a guest powder room, an expansive laundry, a double garage with two large storage rooms and secure ground-floor parking with a generous turning bay, a rare offering in apartment living.\r\n\r\nHeld by one family since it was built in the early 2000s and impeccably maintained, this is lock-and-leave waterfront living moments from St Heliers village’s restaurants, cafés, bars and beach. The vendors have moved, presenting a genuinely rare opportunity to secure one of St Heliers’ finest waterfront residences.\r\n\r\nKey Features:\r\n\r\n• Boutique building of only three residences\r\n• North-west facing views from the Sky Tower to Rangitoto and North Head\r\n• Approx. 240m² of elegant living across two living areas\r\n• Floor-to-ceiling glass from both living areas and the main bedroom\r\n• Formal lounge with gas fireplace, flowing to a covered deck\r\n• Private main wing with balcony access, walk-in wardrobe and statement bathroom\r\n• Two further bedrooms, each with its own bathroom\r\n• Double garage, two large storage rooms and secure parking with turning bay\r\n• Solid concrete block construction, built in the early 2000s\r\n• Moments from St Heliers village and beach",
